.TH "SERIALPORT.DISCONNECT_EVENT" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.disconnect_event \- SerialPort: disconnect event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]disconnect\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
interface is fired when the port disconnects from the device.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqdisconnect\(dq, (event) => { })

ondisconnect = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[CR]disconnect\f[R] event fires when a port that was previously
logically connected to the device is no longer connected.
.SS Bubbling
This event bubbles up to the \f[CR]Serial\f[R] instance that returned
this interface.
The \f[CR]event.target\f[R] property refers to the \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
object that bubbles up.
.PP
For more information, see Event bubbling.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Notify when a specific port disconnects
Here the event listener is installed on a specific \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
object.
.IP
.EX
port.addEventListener(\(dqdisconnect\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// notify that the port has become unavailable\f[R]
});
.EE
.SS Listening for any ports that become unavailable
The \f[CR]disconnect\f[R] event bubbles up to the \f[CR]Serial\f[R]
object where you can listen for any ports that become unavailable.
.IP
.EX
navigator.serial.addEventListener(\(dqdisconnect\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// notify that a port has become unavailable\f[R]
  \f[I]// use \(gaevent.target\(ga to refer to the unavailable port\f[R]
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]connect\f[R] event
